    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Lesbian, gay, bisexual, and transgender high school students face challenges that impede their\r\nacademic, social, and emotional wellbeing. School policies that provide resources and\r\nprotections for LGBT students mitigate these challenges, and lead to better outcomes for LGBT\r\nstudents. LGBT adults face challenges in sectors like employment protection and hate crime\r\nprevalence, and many states have passed laws that expand protections for these adults. This\r\nthesis aims to investigate the relationship between state-level, anti-LGBT discrimination policies\r\nand high-school student wellbeing by analyzing patterns of policy diffusion and the policies’\r\neffects on schools. Using a mixed methods approach that combines linear regression analysis\r\nwith qualitative social research of two school district case studies, this analysis will provide\r\nevidence on the social benefit of expansive civil rights legislation for LGBT individuals and the\r\nspread of its externalities to schools.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Fields, X. (2022). The Influence of Anti-LGBT Discrimination Laws on SchoolClimate and Outcomes for LGBT Youth. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/md834dx5450",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
